<header><p class="enc-kicker">People / group</p><h1 class="enc-title">Tigray People's Liberation Front</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates"><a href="/years/1975">1975</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/20th-century">20th century</a> · Also known as TPLF</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Tigray People's Liberation Front is a political party and former <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/guerrilla-warfare">guerrilla</a> movement founded in 1975 in the Tigray region of northern <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ethiopia">Ethiopia</a>. It led the armed struggle against the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/derg">Derg</a> and dominated the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ethiopian-peoples-revolutionary-democratic-front">EPRDF</a> coalition that took power in 1991, with its leader <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/meles-zenawi">Meles Zenawi</a> heading the government until his death in 2012. After breaking with <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/abiy-ahmed">Abiy Ahmed</a>'s government it fought the Tigray War of 2020–2022.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/tigray-peoples-liberation-front.jpg" alt="Tigray People's Liberation Front" width="320" height="320" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Felipe Fidelis Tobias · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Emblem_Of_Tigray_People%27s_Liberation_Front.svg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
